## 1. Display sale end time in recipient's timezone

```liquid
{% assign sale_end_utc = "2026-08-25 23:59:59" | date: "%s" %}
{% assign recipient_tz = customer.timezone | default: "America/New_York" %}
{{ sale_end_utc | date: "%B %e at %l:%M %p %Z", timezone: recipient_tz }}
```

This converts a UTC timestamp to the customer's IANA timezone. If `timezone` is missing, it falls back to Eastern.

## 2. Change copy after sale ends

```liquid
{% assign sale_end_utc = "2026-08-25 23:59:59" | date: "%s" %}
{% assign now = "now" | date: "%s" %}

{% if now < sale_end_utc %}
  <h1>⚡ Flash Sale: 30% Off Ends {{ sale_end_utc | date: "%B %e at %l:%M %p %Z", timezone: customer.timezone }}</h1>
  <p>Hurry! Only {{ sale_end_utc | minus: now | divided_by: 3600 }} hours left</p>
  <a href="https://shop.example.com/sale">Shop Now</a>
{% else %}
  <h1>You Missed Our Flash Sale</h1>
  <p>The sale has ended, but here are other ways to save...</p>
  <a href="https://shop.example.com/deals">View Current Offers</a>
{% endif %}
```

## 3. Safe first name personalization in subject

```liquid
{% if customer.first_name and customer.first_name != "" %}
{{ customer.first_name }}, flash sale ends soon! ⚡
{% else %}
Flash sale ends soon! ⚡
{% endif %}
```

Or more concise:

```liquid
{% assign name = customer.first_name | default: "" %}
{% if name != "" %}{{ name }}, {% endif %}Flash sale ends soon! ⚡
```

